  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 6,7,3',4'-Tetramethoxyisoflavone and U373 MG, a cancer cell line, through multiple indirect pathways. The compound is linked to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a target of both (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one and Palmyramide A. Palmyramide A is itself a target of U373 MG, indicating a possible role for 6,7,3',4'-Tetramethoxyisoflavone in modulating the activity of these targets. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with varying degrees of support from different targets. The evidence highlights the compound's potential to influence cellular processes through interactions with proteasomal and microtubular pathways, which may contribute to its effect on U373 MG. The integration of these pathways underscores the compound's potential as a modulator of cellular functions in this context.",
